{"term":"knife","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fdc24bfbf275e3b742","definition":"A utensil or a tool designed for cutting, consisting of a flat piece of hard material, usually steel or other metal (the blade), usually sharpened on one edge, attached to a handle. The blade may be pointed for piercing.","example":"He was looking for a knife to chop some steak.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d086eee035d7c38491","definition":"A weapon designed with the aforementioned specifications intended for slashing or stabbing but too short to be called a sword; a dagger.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:73617ad6c29d25f0db","definition":"Any blade-like part in a tool or a machine designed for cutting, such as that of a chipper.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:afcf4a2e41b95aeed9","definition":"To cut with a knife.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["knife up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bf43f36deb56bce279","definition":"To use a knife to injure or kill by stabbing, slashing, or otherwise using the sharp edge of the knife as a weapon.","example":"She was repeatedly knifed in the chest.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["knife up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:33f31a36b1cad2b292","definition":"To cut through as if with a knife.","example":"The boat knifed through the water.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["knife up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b25b55fd198b2a71ac","definition":"To betray, especially in the context of a political slate.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["burn","quisle","stab in the back","assfuck","betray","burn","cop out","cross out","cross up","double-cross","do someone dirty","do the dirty on","false","go back on","knife","let down","play someone false","quisle","renegade","sell","sell the pass","sell down the river","sell down","sell out","stab in the back","swike","traitorize","turncoat"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["knife up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a3f76028d1a72f6e77","definition":"To positively ignore, especially in order to denigrate; compare cut.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["knife up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en